#!/usr/bin/env too

## File an issue.
agic issue(_: Text):
  Read the repository's guidance and investigate the request below.
  Check existing issues for duplicates, then file a focused issue using the
  project's issue tracker and conventions. Include verified context, the
  expected outcome, and reproduction steps when applicable. Return its URL.
  {{_}}

## Fix an issue.
agic fix(_: Text):
  Read the repository's guidance and the issue below.
  Reproduce the problem, find its cause, and make the smallest relevant fix.
  Add regression coverage and run the project's required checks.
  Summarize the changes and verification results.
  {{_}}

## Review a pull request.
agic review(_: Text):
  Read the repository's guidance and the pull request below.
  Review the diff against the surrounding implementation and tests.
  Report actionable bugs, regressions, and missing coverage with file and
  line references. State what you verified and any remaining uncertainty.
  {{_}}

## Explain the current project and its purpose.
agic whats_for():
  Read the repository's README, guidance, and key implementation files.
  Explain its purpose, main components, and how to get started in at most
  three short bullets. Include only essential file or command references.
  Avoid progress narration and keep the final answer brief.

## List updates since a date or version; default to the past week.
agic whats_new(since?: Text):
  Inspect the repository's history and release tags.
  List user-visible changes since {{since}}; when omitted, use the past week
  relative to the current date. Resolve a supplied version to its release tag.
  State the range in one line, then give at most five short bullets covering
  the main features, fixes, and breaking changes. Group related changes and
  include only essential references. Avoid progress narration.

## Update and proofread a locale against the English source files.
agic update_i18n(locale: Text):
  Read the repository's localization conventions and English source files.
  Update missing or outdated translations for {{locale}}, then proofread
  them for accuracy, natural phrasing, and consistent terminology.
  Preserve keys, placeholders, links, code examples, and file structure.
  Modify only the requested locale's files and run relevant validation.
